caption: LinkItem
title: LinkItem
tags: Documentation [[HyperGSD API]]

! Summary
Render a fragment after any GSD link to another tiddler by tagging a tiddler with `$:/tags/hypergsd/LinkItem`.

! Detail
Where the [[ListItem|ListItem Prefix and Suffix]] tag lists adorn a list row's ''own item'', LinkItems adorn a ''link target''. The shared `hgsd-link-items(linked-tiddler)` procedure is placed after the link by every host — `$hgsd.pick-field`'s set state (between the value link and the change button), and the prerequisites/dependants rows. Members receive `linked-tiddler` (the link target's title) with the ambient scope intact.

| !Member | !Adornment |
|`ui/link-items/realm` |the cross-realm globe — the target falls outside the review sidebar's current realm selection (gated by `$:/config/hypergsd/realm-warning`) |

!! Rules
* ''Settings'': the Fragments tab drag-reorders members and toggles per-member visibility (`$:/config/hypergsd/LinkItem/visibility/<title>`, default show). Untagging removes a member from every link surface at once.
* ''Order'': the tag tiddler's `list` field pins members; unlisted members append alphabetically.
* ''Panel and modal share one tag list'': members are read-only adornments; a fragment that must distinguish contexts self-gates on the ambient `section-mode`.
* ''Layout'': every host renders members inside the `hgsd-link-items` container (stylesheet `.hgsd-link-items` — inline-flex, centred, `vertical-align: middle`), so a member is vertically centred in text flow and flex hosts alike; carry no alignment CSS of your own.
* ''Escape hatch'': `$hgsd.pick-field` accepts `link-items="hide"` for hosts that want no adornments.